 get with a  full-blown laptop  but still there's gonna be few cases  that you're gonna find yourself eight  hours away  from a power supply but don't plan on  taking this thing  on a long train journey or a plane  and getting the whole journey worth of  gaming out of it  something else i noticed while using  this thing as well is that while playing  games the thing will  get pretty hot and hand-in-hand with  that  a little noisy not as hot and not as  noisy as you might expect  and not nearly as hot and noisy some  devices that i've used in the past  but definitely enough to take notice now  just before i jump back to my  opening statement and close this video  off i wanted to point out  something that i only just noticed and  this thing is a  fingerprint magnet it's it's real  stylish i  i like the the chassis and i think it  looks super cool  i polished this thing at the start of  this video just before i hit record  and it is already an absolute mess  so i've come full circle back to my  opening statement  the whole jack of all trades thing this  sits  in the middle somewhere somewhere  between the ultra light word processor  web browser  photoshop machine and a intense  mobile gaming rig but  it doesn't do any of them perfectly  this is something that if you want  something very light and portable and  you want  more power when it comes to like video  editing  photoshop if you want something for just  emails word processing on the go  and you want some gaming on top of that  then i think this is the device for you  if you do want to save some weight and  you don't want to carry  a heavy gaming laptop because  those things can weigh a hefty amount  and i think this is going to fit a niche  for you  but unfortunately i think that's what it  is it is a niche  it does a lot of the things it offers  really great and often surprisingly well  especially like i said when it's so  small  thin and light having a  fast display in there its own dedicated  gpu  and getting 